# Git and GitHub Workflow Standards

## Git Operations

- Use git CLI for all operations
- Implement proper error handling for Git commands
- Handle authentication securely

## Branch Management

- Create feature branches for changes
- Use descriptive branch names (e.g., `feat/dark-mode`, `fix/mobile-nav`)
- Implement proper branch cleanup after merge
- Handle branch conflicts appropriately

## PR Operations

- Create PRs with descriptive titles and descriptions
- Include summary, test plan, and relevant screenshots
- Reference related issues in PR description

## Commit Standards

- Use conventional commit messages:
  - `feat:` for new features
  - `fix:` for bug fixes
  - `docs:` for documentation
  - `style:` for formatting/styling
  - `refactor:` for code refactoring
  - `perf:` for performance improvements
  - `test:` for tests
  - `chore:` for maintenance tasks
- Keep commits focused and atomic
- Include relevant context in commit messages

## Error Handling

- Handle network failures gracefully
- Implement proper retry logic for API calls
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log Git and GitHub operations appropriately
